@vilmibm Good question about the `pkg` directory! I forgot to explain.

It's the convention of the Go community to nest sub-packages in `pkg/`. This is not limited to, but especially formalized in [the “Standard” Layout](https://github.com/golang-standards/project-layout#pkg), which we [loosely follow at github](https://github.com/github/go-lang/blob/master/docs/style-guide.md#directory-structure-and-filenames-layout).

I wanted to start setting up a project layout that would encourage us to do package "over-splitting" (as opposed to maintaining large packages that have lots of responsibilities) and I think it would be beneficial if we didn't put all packages at the project's root level (as we did up until now).
